Source: villagesql
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: VillageSQL Contributors <info@villagesql.com>
Homepage: https://villagesql.com
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake (>= 3.14.3),
               g++,
               bison,
               libssl-dev,
               libncurses-dev,
               zlib1g-dev,
               libtirpc-dev,
               rpcsvc-proto,
               libcurl4-openssl-dev,
               libaio-dev,
               libsystemd-dev,
               systemd-dev | systemd,
               pkg-config,
               perl

Package: villagesql-server
Architecture: any
Depends: villagesql-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         villagesql-client (= ${binary:Version}),
         adduser,
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
# Drop-in replacement: anything depending on a MySQL server is satisfied.
Provides: mysql-server, virtual-mysql-server, virtual-mysql-server-core,
          mysql-server-8.4, default-mysql-server
# VillageSQL ships /usr/sbin/mysqld, /var/lib/mysql and mysql.service under the
# same names as MySQL, so it cannot be co-installed with any of these. Breaks +
# Replaces (not just Conflicts) is what lets apt resolve this as a takeover
# rather than refusing the transaction.
Conflicts: mysql-server-5.7, mysql-server-8.0, mysql-server-8.4,
           mysql-server-core-5.7, mysql-server-core-8.0, mysql-server-core-8.4,
           mariadb-server, mariadb-server-10.6, mariadb-server-10.11,
           mariadb-server-core-10.6, mariadb-server-core-10.11,
           percona-server-server, default-mysql-server, default-mysql-server-core
Breaks: mysql-server, mysql-community-server, mariadb-server, percona-server-server
Replaces: mysql-server, mysql-server-5.7, mysql-server-8.0, mysql-server-8.4,
          mysql-server-core-5.7, mysql-server-core-8.0, mysql-server-core-8.4,
          mysql-community-server, mariadb-server,
          mariadb-server-core-10.6, mariadb-server-core-10.11,
          percona-server-server,
          default-mysql-server, default-mysql-server-core
Description: VillageSQL database server binary and configuration
 VillageSQL is an open-source tracking fork of upstream @VSQL_CODE_BASE@ that
 adds the VillageSQL Extension Framework (VEF), a runtime extension system for
 custom SQL data types and functions. VillageSQL tracks several upstream code
 bases; this package was built from @VSQL_CODE_BASE@.
 .
 This package provides the mysqld binary, the systemd unit and the server-side
 utilities. It is wire-, protocol- and on-disk-compatible with upstream
 @VSQL_CODE_BASE@ and installs the same paths and the same systemd unit
 name, so it REPLACES an existing MySQL, MariaDB or Percona Server install
 rather than sitting alongside it.
 .
 Extensions are packaged as .veb bundles, installed at runtime with
 "INSTALL EXTENSION <name>", and loaded from /usr/lib/mysql/veb.

Package: villagesql-client
Architecture: any
Depends: villagesql-common (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: mysql-client, virtual-mysql-client, virtual-mysql-client-core,
          mysql-client-8.4, default-mysql-client
Conflicts: mysql-client-5.7, mysql-client-8.0, mysql-client-8.4,
           mysql-client-core-5.7, mysql-client-core-8.0, mysql-client-core-8.4,
           mariadb-client, mariadb-client-core-10.6, mariadb-client-core-10.11,
           default-mysql-client, default-mysql-client-core
Breaks: mysql-client, mariadb-client
Replaces: mysql-client, mysql-client-5.7, mysql-client-8.0, mysql-client-8.4,
          mysql-client-core-5.7, mysql-client-core-8.0, mysql-client-core-8.4,
          mariadb-client, mariadb-client-core-10.6, mariadb-client-core-10.11,
          default-mysql-client, default-mysql-client-core
Description: VillageSQL command line client and administration tools
 The mysql command line client plus mysqladmin, mysqldump, mysqlimport,
 mysqlshow, mysqlslap, mysqlbinlog and related administration tools.

Package: villagesql-common
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Provides: mysql-common
Conflicts: mysql-common, mariadb-common
Replaces: mysql-common, mariadb-common
Breaks: mysql-common, mariadb-common
Description: VillageSQL shared configuration, character sets and error messages
 Files shared by the VillageSQL server and client packages: /etc/mysql/my.cnf,
 character set definitions and localized error messages.

Package: libvillagesqlclient24
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends: villagesql-common (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: libmysqlclient24, mysql-libs
Conflicts: libmysqlclient21, libmysqlclient24
Replaces: libmysqlclient21, libmysqlclient24
Description: VillageSQL client library
 The libmysqlclient shared library, used by client applications to connect to
 a VillageSQL or MySQL server.

Package: libvillagesqlclient-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: libvillagesqlclient24 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Provides: libmysqlclient-dev, default-libmysqlclient-dev
Conflicts: libmysqlclient-dev, libmariadb-dev
Replaces: libmysqlclient-dev, libmariadb-dev, default-libmysqlclient-dev
Description: VillageSQL client library development files
 Headers, static libraries and mysql_config, for building client applications
 against the VillageSQL client library.
 .
 This package is for CLIENT development. To build VillageSQL EXTENSIONS,
 install villagesql-sdk instead.

Package: villagesql-sdk
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: VillageSQL Extension Framework SDK
 Headers, CMake integration and a template project for building VillageSQL
 extensions (.veb bundles) against the VillageSQL Extension Framework.
 .
 Two header trees are installed: the stable protocol under
 /usr/include/mysql/villagesql and the in-development protocol under
 /usr/include/mysql-dev/villagesql. Build against the stable tree unless you
 are developing the framework itself.
 .
 This package does not depend on villagesql-server: extensions are commonly
 cross-built on a machine that does not run the database.

Package: villagesql-extension-examples
Architecture: all
Depends: villagesql-server (>= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Example VillageSQL extension bundles
 Reference extension bundles shipped with VillageSQL: vsql_simple (a minimal
 custom type and function), vsql_complex (complex number arithmetic with custom
 hash and serialization handlers) and vsql_tvector.
 .
 Installed into /usr/lib/mysql/veb and enabled per-database with, for example,
 "INSTALL EXTENSION vsql_complex;".

Package: villagesql-test
Architecture: any
Depends: villagesql-server (= ${binary:Version}),
         villagesql-client (= ${binary:Version}),
         perl, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: mysql-testsuite
Conflicts: mysql-testsuite, mysql-testsuite-8.0, mysql-testsuite-8.4
Replaces: mysql-testsuite, mysql-testsuite-8.0, mysql-testsuite-8.4
Description: VillageSQL test suite
 The mysql-test-run.pl harness and the full regression suite, including the
 VillageSQL-specific suites under mysql-test/suite/villagesql.
